# Pre-push: full quality gate before code reaches origin. `npm run verify`
# runs scripts/run-gate.mjs, which runs every check the gate has ever run —
# format:check, both workspaces' lint / typecheck / test:coverage (tests *and*
# the coverage floors, exactly what CI's Test Frontend / Test Backend jobs
# run), i18n, settled-read-state ratchets, observability, the production
# dependency audit, the bare-marker and silenced-gate greps, docs/testing.md,
# figures, API spec, sitemap and brand — but concurrently instead of in a
# fifteen-link `&&` chain: measured at 98s and 123s on a busy 10-core laptop
# against 305s for the chain. The step list is scripts/gate-steps.mjs; a
# failure in any one of them fails the push and names itself. These are the
# same stages CI runs (see CICD-27 / CONTRIBUTING.md), so a green pre-push
# almost always means a green CI run.
#
# The cheap checks are unscheduled and report in the first few seconds, so a
# bare marker or a stale doc no longer waits behind the test suites.
#
# If the machine is already busy, `GATE_JOBS=2 git push` narrows the pool;
# `npm run verify -- --jobs 1` reproduces close to the old serial behaviour.
#
# To skip in an emergency: `git push --no-verify`. Don't make this a habit.
npm run verify
